{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrqsYWLo8jLPTjN243A7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote ADR-010 and added it to the ADR index, committed as `958e570`. Lint is clean and the full browser suite (`npm test`) passes, 440 of 440.\n\nThe ADR is `docs/adr/ADR-010-preact-adapter-ownership-split.md`. It has context, decision, rejected alternatives, trade-offs and consequences sections covering every point in the ticket. It links to ADR-004, ADR-005 and ADR-009, and says no ADR is superseded. The index row is dated 2026-11-08 and uses the link-reference style of rows 006 to 009.\n\nI took two claims out of my first draft because they went beyond the spec:\n- **An extra render on client-only mount:** this was wrong. Preact clears the host before inserting it, so nothing has rendered yet.\n- **Prop types that can't go through an attribute being the real edge:** this was a guess.\n\nThe props-before-definition edge is recorded only as the spec states it.\n\n`npm test` first failed with type errors because this fresh worktree had no `dist/`. It passed after `npm run build`, which matches what AGENTS.md already says about fresh worktrees.\n\nI skipped test-first because this ticket is only docs, and recorded that in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed. I left AGENTS.md alone because nothing reusable came out of this ticket.\n\n[x] `docs/adr/ADR-010-preact-adapter-ownership-split.md` exists with context, decision, trade-offs and consequences sections covering every point above.\n[x] `docs/adr/INDEX.md` lists ADR-010 dated 2026-11-08.\n[x] The ADR uses the `CONTEXT.md` meanings of **Hydration** (the intent) and **Adopt** (the mechanism), and says the adapter keeps Preact from undoing hydration without adopting anything itself.\n[x] `npm run lint` passes; the ADR contains no em dashes and no arrow characters."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"us